{
  "rationale": "The plant models robot sensing and actuation, separating perception and motion. The specification enforces conservative, deterministic exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward only after random_walk, and strict turn-based recovery on obstacles. Obstacle events force immediate turn recovery, with left/right obstacles biasing turn direction. No forward or random_walk is allowed in obstacle states. All uncontrollables are total, and only one controllable is enabled per state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception (sensors) and motion (actuators)",
    "Specification automaton binds perception outcomes to safe, deterministic actions, enforcing conservative obstacle recovery and steady exploration"
  ],
